{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794790127,"nonce":"MoXpmNFA113Z+p1yVDlXwTibOCs=","message":"Amended to 155458a: main now runs on a pthread in a threaded Emscripten build (-sPROXY_TO_PTHREAD), as an Ash program runs in a Worker, so await works in a web page and the page's thread stays free to start threads asked for on workers. examples/downloads, which deadlocked threaded in a page before, passes. Three things this needed: (1) Emscripten ends only the thread when a callback on a pthread leaves nothing keeping the runtime alive, so the program never exited after a then callback (primes); hxn.native.Emscripten now exits after a last turn with nothing due and no keepalive. (2) The proxied main thread is strongly referenced under node until cleaned up, which exit() does not do with EXIT_RUNTIME off, so node never exited; threaded builds link with -sEXIT_RUNTIME=1. (3) The canvas has to be transferred to main's pthread with -sOFFSCREENCANVAS_SUPPORT, but that fails at startup without a canvas (under node), so a library that draws adds it under a new link-args key, wasm32-unknown-emscripten-threads, which adds to wasm32-unknown-emscripten's; hxn-gpu-webgl2 and hxn-gpu-webgpu do (local commits, ignored by their current hxn pin).\n\nRun: examples emcc-threads three times under node and emcc-threads-page in Chrome, all pass; counter emcc, gen-emcc, emcc-threads, gen-emcc-threads; tests/web node, browser, node-threads, browser-threads; examples emcc and emcc-page; hxn-gpu-webgl2 and hxn-gpu-webgpu checks cpp --wasm --threads --browser with the canvas on main's pthread.","files":null}]}